WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:18.410
"I hope Zing stays and waits at the Hollow," Zann said.

2
00:00:18.411 --> 00:00:23.837
"I know he wanted to come along. But I'm afraid he'd attract too much attention."

3
00:00:23.838 --> 00:00:28.543
Zann and his friends were walking to town. Dawn was breaking over the swamp.

4
00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:34.606
The aurora birds were singing, and lights were coming on in the outlying homes the kids were passing.

5
00:00:34.607 --> 00:00:38.339
Darb shrugged. "I did my best to convince him to stay."

6
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:48.641
That wasn't very comforting. The dragon could be unpredictable, plus Zann knew that Zing, like all magical creatures, hated being anywhere near the Hollow.

7
00:00:48.642 --> 00:00:51.661
Still, there wasn't much he could do about it.

8
00:00:51.662 --> 00:00:56.978
They were soon in the more populated part of town. "Be careful," Zann warned.

9
00:00:56.979 --> 00:01:01.966
"We don't know what's been going on around here since we went into hiding yesterday."

10
00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:05.756
Gliss rubbed her stomach. "Was it only yesterday?

11
00:01:05.757 --> 00:01:08.834
I feel as if I haven't eaten in days!"

12
00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:12.456
"Me too. But we can eat later," Zann said.

13
00:01:12.457 --> 00:01:16.398
"First we need to get to my house and look for that diary.

14
00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:20.267
And quickly, because Morb could have spies anywhere."

15
00:01:20.268 --> 00:01:28.368
Just then a door slammed nearby. A dragon scurried into the street and let out a yip and a puff of steam.

16
00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:34.105
It was a vapor bounder, a popular breed due to its small size and friendly disposition.

17
00:01:34.106 --> 00:01:40.412
"Hazi, stop!" a voice called. A kid rushed out of the house and scooped up the lively dragon.

18
00:01:40.413 --> 00:01:47.899
"It's Jev!" Gliss exclaimed. Before Zann could stop her, she rushed forward, calling his name. "Jev!"

19
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:52.805
Their classmate turned, looking surprised. "Gliss!" he exclaimed.

20
00:01:52.806 --> 00:01:57.584
"You're okay! Everyone heard your parents are . . . you know . . . gone.

21
00:01:57.585 --> 00:02:00.221
We assumed whoever took them took you too."

22
00:02:00.222 --> 00:02:05.125
"He almost did," Gliss said. "Zann and Darb and Perda saved me."

23
00:02:05.126 --> 00:02:08.363
"Oh." Jev glanced at the others as they caught up.

24
00:02:08.364 --> 00:02:11.009
"Yeah, we thought Zann got nabbed too.

25
00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.547
Especially after what happened to his house."

26
00:02:13.548 --> 00:02:19.397
Jev's tone made it very clear that he wasn't particularly concerned about the loss of Zann's house.

27
00:02:19.398 --> 00:02:23.955
"If you'll excuse us, we've got something important to do," said Zann.

28
00:02:23.956 --> 00:02:30.503
Jev ignored him. "I can't believe you guys are still around," he said, talking mostly to Gliss and Perda.

29
00:02:30.504 --> 00:02:32.944
"Most of the Reds in town are gone.

30
00:02:32.945 --> 00:02:37.960
The only ones left are the mayor and a couple of others who are hiding out with her at the town hall."

31
00:02:37.961 --> 00:02:41.965
"So Morb hasn't broken the mayor's Shield spell?" Gliss asked.

32
00:02:41.966 --> 00:02:44.467
"Who's Morb?" Jev said.

33
00:02:44.468 --> 00:02:48.391
"He's the guy who's been taking all the Reds," Perda explained.

34
00:02:48.392 --> 00:02:52.019
"Wait," Zann put in. "We don't have time to—"

35
00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.922
It was too late. The girls told Jev everything they'd found out.

36
00:02:55.923 --> 00:03:01.073
Zann felt anxious as he listened. He didn't like the idea of telling his enemy all their secrets.

37
00:03:01.074 --> 00:03:05.820
"Wait," Jev said. "Are you telling me this Morb guy is a Void?"

38
00:03:05.821 --> 00:03:13.865
He glanced at Darb and smirked. "No way. Everyone knows Voids are useless at magic and most other things too."

39
00:03:13.866 --> 00:03:20.838
Darb didn't respond. Zann clenched his fists to stop himself from giving Jev another set of donkey ears.

40
00:03:20.839 --> 00:03:24.556
"We need to keep moving," he told his friends.

41
00:03:24.557 --> 00:03:31.817
"You'd better be careful," Jev said. "A bunch of tiny, weird-looking dragons have been flying around town stinging people."

42
00:03:31.818 --> 00:03:38.641
"Stinging dragons?" Darb spoke for the first time since they'd bumped into Jev. "What do they look like?"

43
00:03:38.642 --> 00:03:41.788
"Don't ask me; I didn't see them," Jev said.

44
00:03:41.789 --> 00:03:47.181
"But I heard they swarmed the school last night and grabbed some papers or something from the office."

45
00:03:47.182 --> 00:03:53.031
Darb looked at Zann. "Those could be the same tiny dragons we saw in the swamp yesterday."

46
00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:59.304
Zann shrugged. "Maybe," he said. "But listen, we really need to get moving."

47
00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:03.121
"Zann's right," Perda said. She turned to Jev.

48
00:04:03.122 --> 00:04:06.503
"Will you do me a favor and tell my family that I'm okay?"

49
00:04:06.504 --> 00:04:10.311
"Mine too," Darb put in quietly. "Please?"

50
00:04:10.312 --> 00:04:12.773
"Why should I?" said Jev.

51
00:04:12.774 --> 00:04:18.864
"Please, Jev," said Gliss. "My parents would be going crazy with worry if it were me."

52
00:04:18.865 --> 00:04:22.645
Her lower lip trembled. "If they were still around, I mean."

53
00:04:22.646 --> 00:04:27.345
"Okay, okay," Jev said quickly. "I was just kidding. I'll tell them."

54
00:04:27.346 --> 00:04:32.922
Just then the dragon in his arms wriggled loose. "Hey! Get back here, Hazi!"

55
00:04:32.923 --> 00:04:39.202
He rubbed his hands together, conjuring up a dragon harness. Then he chased after his pet.

56
00:04:39.203 --> 00:04:45.979
Zann grimaced. It felt strange to know that he couldn't even conjure up something as simple as that harness right now.

57
00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:49.897
He wasn't used to living without magic. How did Darb do it?

58
00:04:49.898 --> 00:04:55.164
"Let's go," he told his friends. "We've wasted enough time already."

59
00:04:55.165 --> 00:05:02.645
Soon they were several blocks away. "We should have asked Jev to conjure some breakfast for us," Perda said.

60
00:05:02.646 --> 00:05:09.208
"Oh!" Gliss stopped short. "Why didn't I think of that? Maybe we should go back."

61
00:05:09.209 --> 00:05:16.243
Zann stopped too. "We don't have time." Just then his stomach grumbled and he thought of something.

62
00:05:16.244 --> 00:05:21.418
"Why are we assuming that Perda can't use magic? She's not a Red.

63
00:05:21.419 --> 00:05:25.369
I'm sure it's safe for her to conjure some breakfast for us."

64
00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:29.951
"Do you really think that's a good idea?" Darb seemed dubious.

65
00:05:29.952 --> 00:05:35.962
"That makes total sense, Zann!" said Gliss. "Morb's only after Reds, right?

66
00:05:35.963 --> 00:05:40.587
Perda can probably do all the magic she wants, and Morb won't care at all."

67
00:05:40.588 --> 00:05:45.161
Perda licked her lips. "How do puckerberry pancakes sound?"

68
00:05:45.162 --> 00:05:48.064
"Great," Zann said. "But hurry."

69
00:05:48.065 --> 00:05:52.156
Perda rubbed her hands together, and then held them facing upward.

70
00:05:52.157 --> 00:05:58.193
A second later a steaming platter of food appeared. "Yum!" Gliss exclaimed.

71
00:05:58.194 --> 00:06:06.875
Just then a large, hulking figure appeared, casting a dark shadow over everyone. Then another figure appeared. And another.

72
00:06:06.876 --> 00:06:19.170
Perda screamed and dropped the plate of food, which shattered at her feet. "Trolls!" she cried.
